pyra-sound (0.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The tooltip and the bar show one volume, the wheel's position, the same
    on the speakers and the headphones: 0% at the bottom stop, 100% at the
    top. The speaker range comes from the running pyra_volumed (range in
    /etc/pyra_volumed.conf for pyra-hacks' daemon).

 -- pyra-sound maintainers <pyra-sound@example.invalid>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

pyra-sound (0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The right-click window shows the playing output's volume as a read-only
    bar that follows the wheel.
  * pyra-hacks' pyra_volumed from 0.38+pyra2 on is recognised as driving the
    headphones, so the headphone slider no longer shows with it.

 -- pyra-sound maintainers <pyra-sound@example.invalid>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000

pyra-sound (0.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * pactl subscribe and alsactl monitor now exit with pyra-sound, also at
    logout or when it is killed; 0.1 left them running after every session.

 -- pyra-sound maintainers <pyra-sound@example.invalid>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

pyra-sound (0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: a sound icon for MATE's Notification Area on the Pyra,
    in place of MATE's own, which the package hides at login.
  * Left click mutes; right click chooses the speakers or the headphones.
  * Icon and tooltip show the output and the amplifier volume, and follow
    changes made elsewhere.
  * The volume wheel stays with pyra_volumed. A headphone volume slider
    shows only when the running daemon doesn't drive the headphones.
  * AESS kernels (5.6.19-m4*) only.

 -- pyra-sound maintainers <pyra-sound@example.invalid>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
